## Current implementation

The repository builds a static Astro marketing site, a Markdoc documentation site, a simulated workspace, and a narrow Cloudflare Worker contact handler.

Repository-native secure delivery definitions now include PR policy, quality, security, browser gates, immutable Action pins, artifact digest promotion, manual environment-gated deploy workflows, security policies, and operating runbooks. Unit tests cover the hardened contact boundary.

GitHub ruleset `Protect main` is active on the default branch. It blocks deletion and force pushes, requires pull requests with resolved review conversations, and grants no bypass. Required checks remain intentionally pending until the repository-native PR workflows have completed successfully and GitHub has observed their check names.

GitHub environments, reviewers, isolated deployment secrets, secret scanning, and Cloudflare WAF/rate-limit controls still require external human configuration. No deployment was performed as part of this implementation.

## Simulated orchestration

The orchestration module executes typed local logic only. Its adapters create prompt previews. Its stores are in-memory. It does not run provider CLIs, alter Git branches, persist jobs, send messages, or perform production actions.

## Target architecture

The supplied Tier 1 sources define a brokered company with durable work units, isolated worktrees, real deterministic commands, fresh independent reviewers, majority convergence, human approvals, and auditable outcomes. Those capabilities remain target state unless a current page and test prove otherwise.
